Alembic migrations for PSX Invest.

The database URL is read from application settings (PSX_DATABASE_URL) in env.py,
not from alembic.ini.

Common commands (run from backend/, with the virtualenv active):

    alembic upgrade head                        # apply all migrations
    alembic downgrade -1                        # revert the last one
    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "note"   # generate from model changes
    alembic current                             # show the applied revision
    alembic history --verbose                   # show the full chain

After autogenerating, ALWAYS read the generated file before committing it.
Autogenerate detects added and removed columns; it cannot tell a rename from a
drop-plus-add, and it will silently discard data if you let it.
